  "term": "taurine",
  "definition": "Taurine is a beta-amino acid involved in energy metabolism, inhibitory neurotransmission, calcium balance, and antioxidant protection. In autism research, low taurine levels have been proposed as a possible finding in some individuals, although study results are mixed.",
